# Play’Up web — quality

## Stack (intentional)

| Concern | Tool | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Format | **Prettier** | Not oxfmt/Biome |
| Lint | **Oxlint** | `--deny-warnings`; do **not** add ESLint in parallel |
| Types | `tsc -b` (`npm run typecheck`) | Strict via `tsconfig` |
| CSS lint | **Stylelint** | `lint:css` — `src/**/*.css` (CI); README notes some legacy page CSS intentionally out of scope for DS-only rules |
| Hygiene audits | `frontend:audit`, `i18n:audit:repo`, `css:audit`, `i18n:audit`, `tile:check` | Global + structure-scoped `scripts/`; not CI gates (F1 / F1bis / AUD-0001) |
| Coverage | Vitest V8 | `test:coverage` — measurement only, no CI threshold |

```bash
cd src/PlayUp/web
npm run format:check
npm run lint
npm run lint:css
npm run typecheck
npm run test:run
npm run build
```

CI `web` runs the same gates (then Playwright stub smoke). `npm run build` runs `tsc -b` and catches test-project type errors — do not rely on `typecheck` alone. PR prep: `.cursor/commands/audit-before-pr.md`.

## Data path

- HTTP → **`api.ts` only** (`fetch` lives there). Do not call `fetch` from pages/components.
- Server state → **TanStack Query** (`useQuery` / `useMutation`); do not load API data in `useEffect`.
- Query keys → **`queryKeys.ts`** factory; do not invent parallel key shapes.
- Do not add a second HTTP client or a global client-state library without a demonstrated need.

## Loading UX

Section/tile **initial load** vs **background refresh** → see `loading-states.mdc`.

## Conventions

- Prettier: single quotes, trailing commas, semis, `printWidth` 80 (CSS 120).
- Prefer extracting non-component exports over disabling `only-export-components`.
- Form `onSubmit`: `SubmitEvent`, not deprecated `FormEvent`.
- Source comments: English; current constraints only — see `documentation.mdc`.
